80-bit values copied through the FPU keep all their bits (FILD/FISTP m64 already do, upstream 79ac877): FLD m80
and FLD ST(i) put the exact 80 bits in rawst (as FRSTOR does) instead of converting them to a double, which has 53
bits of mantissa, and FSTP m80 stores them as they are while no instruction has written the register since.

